  {
    "bbox": [
      167.90550231933594,
      47.37071990966797,
      556.248779296875,
      59.5465202331543
    ],
    "text": "Hinze17 and Shinnar and ­Church18 modified the theory of isentropic turbulence by means of an equation "
  },
  {
    "bbox": [
      155.90809631347656,
      57.404541015625,
      556.2383422851562,
      69.54553985595703
    ],
    "text": "with the surface energy produced by the breaking of drops and the kinetic energy caused by the fluctuations of "
  },
  {
    "bbox": [
      155.90809631347656,
      67.403564453125,
      332.5745849609375,
      79.54456329345703
    ],
    "text": "the same drop volume in the vortex on each side."
  },
  {
    "bbox": [
      155.90809631347656,
      115.70654296875,
      556.3001098632812,
      127.84754180908203
    ],
    "text": "where the power loss per unit mass of liquids (ψ) can be calculated by the equation proposed by Jealous and "
  },
  {
    "bbox": [
      155.90809631347656,
      125.67082977294922,
      193.64849853515625,
      137.84657287597656
    ],
    "text": "­Johnson19:"
  },
  {
    "bbox": [
      167.9084930419922,
      178.103515625,
      440.3130187988281,
      190.9125213623047
    ],
    "text": "For the orifice coefficient ­(C0), a constant value of ­C0 = 0.6 is recommended."
  },
  {
    "bbox": [
      167.9225311279297,
      188.1044921875,
      556.1952514648438,
      200.24549865722656
    ],
    "text": "The proposed equations for determining the average diameter of drops based on the Kolmogorov theory "
  },
  {
    "bbox": [
      155.925537109375,
      198.103515625,
      556.3344116210938,
      210.24452209472656
    ],
    "text": "describe the effect of pulsation intensity on the size of the drops and predict the diameter of the drops in the "
  },
  {
    "bbox": [
      155.925537109375,
      208.1025390625,
      554.2672119140625,
      220.24354553222656
    ],
    "text": "range of the mixer-settler regime. Literature missing about the breaking of drops in pulsed sieve-plate extrac-"
  },
  {
    "bbox": [
      155.925537109375,
      218.1015625,
      556.0799560546875,
      230.24256896972656
    ],
    "text": "tion columns show that the breaking of drops when passing through the holes of the mesh tray is caused by "
  },
  {
    "bbox": [
      155.925537109375,
      228.1005859375,
      556.3019409179688,
      240.24159240722656
    ],
    "text": "their shear stress. Anyway, the theory of isotropic turbulence is not suitable for describing the process of drop "
  },
  {
    "bbox": [
      155.925537109375,
      238.07086181640625,
      275.5328063964844,
      250.24647521972656
    ],
    "text": "breaking in mesh tray ­columns20."
  },
  {
    "bbox": [
      167.90179443359375,
      248.1044921875,
      556.2445068359375,
      260.2454833984375
    ],
    "text": "Use On the one hand, new physical models have been proposed to predict drop size in pulsed sieve-plate "
  },
  {
    "bbox": [
      155.90480041503906,
      258.103515625,
      556.2596435546875,
      270.2445068359375
    ],
    "text": "extraction columns. Pietzsch and Pilhofer to model the stability of the drop when passing through the sieve-plate "
  },
  {
    "bbox": [
      155.90480041503906,
      268.1025085449219,
      556.1756591796875,
      280.2434997558594
    ],
    "text": "by equating the drag, buoyancy and inertia forces (which cause the drop to break) with the interphase tension "
  },
  {
    "bbox": [
      155.90480041503906,
      278.0709533691406,
      445.9798889160156,
      290.24658203125
    ],
    "text": "force (which causes the drop to remain stable) gave a relation to have ­achieved21:"
  },
  {
    "bbox": [
      167.90689086914062,
      330.10760498046875,
      556.24609375,
      342.24859619140625
    ],
